  "result": "Perfect! All 159 tests pass. I've successfully implemented payment terms support:\n\n**Added to `src/dates.js`:**\n\n**lastDayOfMonth(date)**\n- Returns the last day of the month for a given date\n- Handles all month lengths (28-31 days)\n- Correctly handles leap years\n- Uses UTC arithmetic\n\n**Updated `src/invoices.js`:**\n\n**createInvoice now accepts optional `terms` parameter:**\n- `'NET14'`: Due 14 days from issue date\n- `'NET30'`: Due 30 days from issue date (default if not specified)\n- `'EOM'`: Due on last day of issue month\n- Unknown terms return TERMS_INVALID error\n\n**Invoice now includes:**\n- `invoice.terms`: The payment term type\n- `invoice.dueDate`: Calculated due date in YYYY-MM-DD format\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`:**\n- Added TERMS_INVALID error code\n\n**Comprehensive tests covering:**\n- Default NET30 terms\n- All three term types (NET14, NET30, EOM)\n- Date calculations:\n  - Across month boundaries\n  - Across year boundaries\n  - Different month lengths (28, 30, 31 days)\n  - Leap year dates\n- Invalid terms rejection\n- Term dates are valid YYYY-MM-DD strings\n\n**Example invoice creation:**\n```javascript\n// Default NET30\ncreateInvoice({\n  customerId: 'C-003',\n  issueDate: '2026-10-07',\n  lines: [...]\n}) // dueDate: '2026-11-06'\n\n// NET14\ncreateInvoice({\n  customerId: 'C-003',\n  issueDate: '2026-10-07',\n  lines: [...],\n  terms: 'NET14'\n}) // dueDate: '2026-10-21'\n\n// EOM\ncreateInvoice({\n  customerId: 'C-003',\n  issueDate: '2026-10-07',\n  lines: [...],\n  terms: 'EOM'\n}) // dueDate: '2026-10-31'\n```",
